# Dependencies and build output must never enter the context. On Windows these
# are Junctions pointing at absolute C:/Users/... paths; copied into the image
# they overwrite pnpm's correct relative symlinks and dangle on Linux, which
# surfaces as "Module not found" for an arbitrary subset of packages. The **
# prefix is explicit because the bare-name patterns below were not reliably
# matching at depth.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
data
__tests__
# NOTE: agent/ is deliberately NOT excluded. pnpm-workspace.yaml declares
# src, web, and agent as workspace packages, and the Dockerfile copies
# agent/package.json into every stage that runs `pnpm install` so the
# workspace matches pnpm-lock.yaml's four importers. Excluding the directory
# would make that copy fail. No stage does `COPY agent/`, so agent source
# still never enters the image.
scripts/
.github/
*.test.ts
vitest.config.ts
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.env
.env.local
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
README.md
LICENSE
ISSUES.md
